      "message": "The structuring here seems a bit weird; it feels like it would be better structured as two functions. `writeFunction` would become basically the new block that you\u0027ve added here; it is responsible for calling `writeFunctionInstantiation`, which is basically the original `writeFunction` code. `writeFunctionInstantiation` would emit one instantiation of a function.  \n\nThis seems cleaner and makes it obvious that the code won\u0027t lead to runaway recursion. (As written, it is far from obvious!) It also does less work since we only need to search the `fSpecializationMap` one time.",
